lattice-catalogue 3
# Hand-written catalogue for tests. A generated tests/fixtures/generated/catalogue.lcat replaces it when present.
# Test values (not game claims): each kit's options run from 0 in the order listed here; the game's pipe, chute
#   and rail kits hold more options between them.
# Game facts: StructureWallIron finishes at state 1,
#   StructureFrameIron and StructureCompositeWindowIron at state 2; the steel frame's states 2 and 3 block air.
# Game facts: ItemCableCoil option order and cost per piece, one build state,
#   exit tool ItemWireCutters, ratings 5000 W normal / 100000 W heavy, the local end directions of each normal shape,
#   long straights (pivot plus N-1 cells along -z, ends +z at the pivot and -z at the far cell).
# From the game catalogue (the catalogue reader's headless export on the test instance): each small
#   piece's ends and footprint cells. Long straights do not all run one way: cables pivot..-z, pipes pivot..+z
#   (StructurePipeStraight3), chutes pivot..-x with x ends (StructureChuteStraight, StructureChuteStraight3), rails
#   pivot..-y (StructureRoboticArmRailStraightStop); the pipe corner's ends are x- and z-.
# Game facts (connection is geometric): the area power control's input at -x, output at +x.
# Game facts: a frame takes its cell's centre slot, a wall one
#   face slot; one slot per kind per small cell; collision classes cables 2, pipes 1,
#   chutes 23, small devices 23, the APC Everything (31), cable fuses 21; cable ends 0.34 m (-) and 0.40 m (+) from
#   centre, pipe ends 0.34 m (-) and 0.37 m (+).
# Test values (not game claims): which face the unturned wall and window take; the chute's and fuse's names, kits
#   and ends.
# Test values (not game claims): the small tank's single cell and y- port (the game's tank fills 3 x 4 x 3 small cells
#   with x+ and z+ ports); the slots of large pieces (the reader gives large pieces no footprint).
# Test values (not game claims): the kits, tools and materials of frames, walls, windows, pipes, the tank and the APC;
#   which states of the iron frame and window block air; pipe ends and ratings; the tank's port and its role;
#   which steps block gravity (the last step of frames, walls and windows).
# Game facts: any IConstructor tool takes a broken structure apart;
#   the game's are ItemAngleGrinder, ItemArcWelder and ItemWeldingTorch.
# Test values (not game claims): one spray can per paint colour 0 to 15, each giving 10 acts.
# Game facts: the game's labeller is ItemLabeller.

broken-tools ItemAngleGrinder,ItemArcWelder,ItemWeldingTorch

item TestSprayCan0 name=Test%20Spray%20Can%200 paint=0 acts=10
item TestSprayCan1 name=Test%20Spray%20Can%201 paint=1 acts=10
item TestSprayCan2 name=Test%20Spray%20Can%202 paint=2 acts=10
item TestSprayCan3 name=Test%20Spray%20Can%203 paint=3 acts=10
